<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vincas Mickevičius-Kapsukas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1935</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vincas Kapsukas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vincas Mickevičius-Kapsukas was a Lithuanian communist leader and writer. He headed the Soviet government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> in 1918–1919 and then chaired the council of people's commissars of the short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-byelorussian-soviet-socialist-republic">Lithuanian–Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic</a>, before working for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Communist International</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p></div>
